; {$modeswitch}: in objfpc mode, result and out turned off (Result and out
; are then ordinary names), and class and exceptions (already on)
; accepted; output as Free Pascal's. Switches that pcc's mode decides or
; always has cannot be changed, those of features pcc lacks cannot be turned
; on, and unknown names and forms are reported (warnings, as Free Pascal's).
; RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t
; RUN: %pcc --mode=objfpc %S/Inputs/modeswitch/resultoff.pas -o %t/resultoff
; RUN: %t/resultoff | FileCheck --check-prefix=OFF %s
; OFF: 15
; RUN: %pcc --mode=tp -c %S/Inputs/modeswitch/warnings.pas -o %t/w.o 2>&1 | FileCheck --check-prefix=TP %s
; TP: warnings.pas:2:1: warning: mode switch 'class' cannot be turned on in --mode=tp; use --mode=objfpc (ignored)
; TP: warnings.pas:3:1: warning: mode switch 'cvar' cannot be turned off; ignored
; TP: warnings.pas:4:1: warning: mode switch 'nestedcomments' is not supported; ignored
; TP-NOT: warnings.pas:5
; TP: warnings.pas:6:1: warning: unknown mode switch 'bogus'; ignored
; TP: warnings.pas:7:1: warning: expected {$modeswitch NAME} (with +, -, ON or OFF); ignored
; TP-NOT: warning:
; RUN: %pcc --mode=objfpc -c %S/Inputs/modeswitch/warnings.pas -o %t/w2.o 2>&1 | FileCheck --check-prefix=OBJFPC %s
; OBJFPC: warnings.pas:8:1: warning: mode switch 'objpas' cannot be turned off in --mode=objfpc; use --mode=tp (ignored)
